==========================================================================
4. WHY THE 42/42 CENSUS MISSED IT (MISTAKE-337)
==========================================================================
  ALL three-cluster configs, d=6..12: 51/2100 fail = 2.43%
  EQUAL-SIZE three-cluster configs only: 0/30 fail = 0.00%
  The original census varied the ROOT RATIOS and the number of clusters but
  held the cluster SIZES equal (d//3 each).  That single un-varied axis is
  exactly the one the failure lives on.  A census that does not vary an axis
  is not evidence about that axis, however large its sample.

==========================================================================
5. FREE-FERMION / BAND-FILLING LOCALIZATION: WHERE the reversals sit
==========================================================================
  e_k is the canonical k-fermion partition function of a system whose
  grand partition function is prod(1 + r_i t): single-particle Boltzmann
  weights r_i, fugacity t.  log h_k is its free energy in the binomial
  gauge and the circuit is the THIRD derivative in particle number k.
  Well-separated clusters are BANDS; filling a band is a first-order
  transition, so reversals must sit at the band-filling numbers, i.e. at
  the partial sums of the cluster sizes with roots sorted DESCENDING.

    sizes (largest root first)  band-filling k   observed reversal sites
    (4, 5, 3)                  [4, 9]          [4, 7, 9]              boundaries hit: True  total=3 (=2m-3: True) exact zeros at []
    (3, 3, 3)                  [3, 6]          [3, 4, 6]              boundaries hit: True  total=3 (=2m-3: True) exact zeros at [5]
    (6, 2, 4)                  [6, 8]          [6, 7, 8]              boundaries hit: True  total=3 (=2m-3: True) exact zeros at []
    (2, 7, 3)                  [2, 9]          [2, 5, 9]              boundaries hit: True  total=3 (=2m-3: True) exact zeros at []
    (5, 4, 2, 3)               [5, 9, 11]      [5, 7, 9, 10, 11]      boundaries hit: True  total=5 (=2m-3: True) exact zeros at []
    (3, 3, 3, 3)               [3, 6, 9]       [3, 4, 6, 8, 9]        boundaries hit: True  total=5 (=2m-3: True) exact zeros at []
    (2, 3, 4, 2, 3)            [2, 5, 9, 11]   [2, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10, 11] boundaries hit: True  total=7 (=2m-3: True) exact zeros at []

  DECOMPOSITION.  Every band boundary is a reversal site, and exactly one
  further reversal sits strictly between each pair of consecutive
  boundaries.  So
        sign changes = (m-1) boundary sites + (m-2) inter-band sites
                     = 2m-3,
  which is a complete structural account of the count in part 2.

  EXACT ZEROS ARE FORCED BY RIGIDITY, NOT EXTRA REVERSALS.  Equal cluster
  sizes with geometric separation make the log-root measure SYMMETRIC, so
  THM-3003 section 1 gives c_k = -c_(d+1-k); when d is odd, k=(d+1)/2 is a
  fixed point of that involution and c vanishes there EXACTLY.  Check:
    sizes (3, 3, 3)      d= 9  exact zeros [5]      predicted [5]      OK
    sizes (2, 2, 2)      d= 6  exact zeros []       predicted []       OK
    sizes (4, 4, 4)      d=12  exact zeros []       predicted []       OK
    sizes (2, 2, 2, 2)   d= 8  exact zeros []       predicted []       OK
  VERDICT 5: LOCALIZATION + FORCED-ZERO CONFIRMED

